  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.5.0 — hardening in lockstep with the family: unwrap rejects oversized wrapped blobs client-side (the KMS Decrypt limit is 6,144 bytes), so a hostile container yields the documented fail-closed PqDecryptionException instead of a raw SDK exception after a doomed network round-trip, and the engine now rejects any provider-returned content key that is not exactly 32 bytes. No change to the provider's API or the .pqfe v2 container format, which remains FROZEN for the 1.x line. See CHANGELOG.md.",
